<p>
    <strong>Inactive accounts.</strong> An account with no sign-in for <strong>3 years</strong> is
    deleted, after prior notice sent to you.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Backups.</strong> Our database backups rotate every <strong>7 days</strong>. Deleted
    data may therefore remain in a backup for at most 7 days; a backup is never restored without
    re-applying deletions.
</p>

<h2>4. Our legitimate interests, in plain terms</h2>
<p>
    Where we rely on "legitimate interests" (Art. 6(1)(f)), this is exactly what we pursue:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>
        <strong>Security and traceability.</strong> Keeping audit logs and the IP addresses tied to
        sessions lets us detect fraudulent access, understand an incident and evidence it.
        Recital 49 GDPR expressly recognises information system security as a legitimate interest.
        These logs are access-restricted, never contain passwords or tokens, and are anonymised
        after one year.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Sharing and collaboration.</strong> When you invite someone to join a house, we
        create a link carrying a time-limited token, which you pass on yourself through the channel
        of your choice. We process no data about the invited person until they create their own
        account. The interest is the sharing feature you asked us to carry out. Invitations have a
        limited lifetime (7 days) and are deleted 30 days after they expire.
    </li>
</ul>
<p>
    You may object to this processing (see § 8). We will consider your request and give you a
    reasoned answer.
</p>

<h2>5. Who has access to your data?</h2>
<p>
    Your data is never sold, rented, or passed on for advertising. Access is limited to:
</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>You</strong>, and the members of a house you share, within the rights granted to them. Invitations are issued by the house owner; a read-and-write collaborator may additionally invite a tenant.</li>
    <li><strong>The HouseFlow team</strong>, strictly as needed to run and support the service, under a confidentiality obligation.</li>
    <li>
        <strong>Microsoft Azure</strong> (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited), our hosting
        provider, acting as a <em>processor</em> under Article 28 GDPR, on the basis of the
        <em>Microsoft Products and Services Data Protection Addendum</em> (DPA).
    </li>
</ul>
<p>
    HouseFlow's source code is hosted on <strong>GitHub</strong>. That hosting contains
    <strong>no</strong> user personal data.
</p>
<p>
    We use <strong>no other processor</strong>: no analytics tool, no third-party emailing service,
    no external monitoring tool. This list will be updated and this policy re-versioned should that
    change.
</p>

<h2>6. Where is your data hosted? Are there transfers outside Europe?</h2>
<p>
    Your data is hosted by Microsoft Azure in the <strong>West Europe</strong> region
    (Netherlands), within the European Economic Area (EEA). Backup replication stays inside the EEA.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>We make no deliberate transfer of your data outside the EEA.</strong> A Microsoft
    support operation may nevertheless involve occasional access from a third country. Such access
    is governed by Microsoft's DPA, which incorporates the European Commission's
    <strong>standard contractual clauses</strong> of 4 June 2021 (Art. 46(2)(c)), and by the
    <strong>EU-US Data Privacy Framework adequacy decision</strong> of 10 July 2023 (Art. 45),
    Microsoft being on the list of certified organisations.
</p>
<p>
    You can obtain a copy of these safeguards by writing to
    <a href="mailto:@LegalConstants.PrivacyContactEmail">@LegalConstants.PrivacyContactEmail</a>.
</p>

<h2>7. What information must you provide?</h2>
<p>
    <strong>Mandatory</strong> — without these the account cannot be created, as they are necessary
    to perform the contract:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>your <strong>email address</strong> (it identifies you and is how you sign in);</li>
    <li>your <strong>last name</strong> and <strong>first name</strong> (they identify you to the people you share a house with);</li>
    <li>a <strong>password</strong> (it protects your account).</li>
</ul>
<p>
    <strong>Optional</strong> — leaving these out costs you no essential feature, only a less
    detailed history: a house's address, a device's brand, model and installation date, the cost of
    a maintenance job, the name of a service provider, and free-text notes.
</p>

<h2>8. Your rights</h2>
<p>You have the following rights over your data, at any time:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Right of access</strong> (Art. 15) — obtain a copy of all the data we hold about you.</li>
    <li><strong>Right to rectification</strong> (Art. 16) — correct inaccurate or incomplete information.</li>
    <li><strong>Right to erasure</strong> (Art. 17) — have your account and your data deleted. Deletion is immediate; an access token already issued may remain technically valid for at most 15 minutes, without giving access to any data, as it has already been deleted.</li>
    <li><strong>Right to restriction</strong> (Art. 18) — ask us to freeze a processing operation, for example while we verify data you contest.</li>
    <li><strong>Right to object</strong> (Art. 21) — object, on grounds relating to your particular situation, to processing based on our legitimate interests (audit logs, invitations).</li>
    <li><strong>Right to data portability</strong> (Art. 20) — receive, in a machine-readable format, the data you provided to us, so you can take it elsewhere.</li>
    <li><strong>Post-mortem instructions</strong> (Art. 85 of the French Data Protection Act) — set instructions on what happens to your data after your death, either general instructions with a certified digital trustee or specific instructions sent to us.</li>
</ul>
<p>
    HouseFlow relies on no consent within the meaning of Article 6(1)(a), so there is no consent to
    withdraw. Should we ever introduce processing based on consent (a newsletter, for instance), it
    would be optional, collected separately, and withdrawable at any time as easily as it was given.
</p>

<h3>How to exercise your rights</h3>
<p>Directly in the app, without writing to us:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Settings → Profile</strong>: view and correct your last name, first name, email and preferences.</li>
    <li><strong>Settings → Export my data</strong>: download all of your data (access and portability).</li>
    <li><strong>Settings → Delete my account</strong>: permanently erase your account and your data.</li>
</ul>
<p>
    Or by email to <a href="mailto:@LegalConstants.PrivacyContactEmail">@LegalConstants.PrivacyContactEmail</a>,
    for any request, including restriction, objection and post-mortem instructions.
</p>
<p>
    We answer <strong>within one month</strong> of receiving your request. That period may be
    extended by two months where the request is complex; we then tell you so, with the reasons,
    within the first month. <strong>Exercising your rights is free of charge.</strong> As you are
    already signed in to the app, we will not ask you for identity documents unless there is
    serious doubt as to your identity.
</p>

