<p>
    <strong>No third-party tracker</strong> (analytics, advertising, session replay, embedded
    content) is used. Should we introduce one, we would deploy a genuine consent management tool,
    with refusing as easy as accepting.
</p>

<h2>12. Minors</h2>
<p>
    HouseFlow is restricted to <strong>adults</strong>. The service is neither intended nor offered
    to minors. For reference, the age at which a minor can consent alone to an online service is
    <strong>15 in France</strong> and <strong>13 in Belgium</strong>.
</p>
<p>
    We do not knowingly collect data about minors. If you notice such an account has been created,
    write to <a href="mailto:@LegalConstants.PrivacyContactEmail">@LegalConstants.PrivacyContactEmail</a>
    and we will delete it.
</p>

<h2>13. How do we protect your data?</h2>
<ul>
    <li>All communication is encrypted with <strong>HTTPS/TLS</strong>.</li>
    <li>Passwords are stored as salted <strong>BCrypt hashes</strong>: they are never kept or recoverable in clear text, including by us.</li>
    <li>Your password must be at least <strong>8 characters</strong>, with a lowercase letter, an uppercase letter, a digit and a special character, in line with the CNIL's recommendation — which allows this length where the number of sign-in attempts is limited, as it is here.</li>
    <li>Access tokens expire after <strong>15 minutes</strong>, and session tokens are rotated on every renewal.</li>
    <li>Access rights to each house are checked <strong>server-side, resource by resource</strong> (owner, collaborator and tenant roles).</li>
    <li>Data is <strong>encrypted at rest</strong> by Azure, and administrative access is named and protected by multi-factor authentication.</li>
    <li>Logs never contain passwords, tokens or API keys.</li>
</ul>

<h2>14. Data about people other than you</h2>
<p>
    When you invite someone to share a house, or when you record a service provider's name in a
    maintenance entry, you pass us data about a third party. We process it on your behalf, on the
    basis of our legitimate interest in making sharing and maintenance tracking work.
</p>
<p>
    Those people have the same rights as you (§ 8) and can write to
    <a href="mailto:@LegalConstants.PrivacyContactEmail">@LegalConstants.PrivacyContactEmail</a>.
    We are unable to inform them individually, having no reliable contact details for them: this
    general information is provided under the exception in Article 14(5)(b) GDPR (disproportionate
    effort). Please enter only genuinely useful information in free-text fields, and never
    sensitive data.
</p>
<p>
    If you delete your account while a house is shared with a collaborator, that house and its
    history are transferred to them, because the data is theirs too, and references naming you are
    anonymised. If the only remaining members are tenants, the house and its history are deleted
    along with your account: a tenant does not inherit ownership.
</p>

